\section{Keep the match record inspectable}

Return the identities of covered operations, ordered inputs and outputs, and any predicates not yet discharged, such as compatible register classes or legal placement. Deduplicate only records interchangeable at that interface: two embeddings covering the same operations might require different operand orders and therefore lead to different encodings. Record why rejected anchors failed, at least in a diagnostic mode. A missing edge, an unencodable immediate and a hidden external use indicate three different problems; maintaining those distinctions helps when a new rule appears to match but never reaches emitted code. Chapter~\ref{ch:ext-276} examines what happens when the candidate itself spans block boundaries.
